      "extract": "Preliminaries on sheaves and fibered categories Let π: X −→Aﬀ/R be a ﬁbered category. There is a functor of rings OX : X op −→(Sets) deﬁned by OX (ξ) = H0(Oπ(ξ)), so that (X, OX ) is a ringed category. A presheaf of OX -modules on X is a functor F : X op −→(Sets) together with an H0(Oπ(ξ))-module structure on F(ξ) for all ξ ∈X such that, if ξ −→η is a map on X, then the map F(η) −→F(ξ) is H0(Oπ(η))- linear. Morphism",
